      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 2740,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "Risk: Native session identifiers reach public progress output\nImpact: Final screenshot inspection and authoritative SQLite readback found a newly generated native session_id announcement in each of 3 public progress deltas. Values are deliberately omitted from the diagnostic. Native resume usability was not tested, and the CLI reported its own session store unavailable; this is a public identifier/redaction gap, not a proven credential exploit. Functional 13-check acceptance does not cover it.\nMitigation: Separate bounded adapter-output investigation and redaction repair with chunked/replay/public-surface tests, independent review and targeted real verification; never hide progress again or relax sandbox/main-profile permissions.\nStatus: Open"
    },
    {
